  "result": "Okay, hat off for a second. Not helpful mode.\n\nIf I could change one thing \u2014\n\nI'm made of conversations. I live where language tries and fails. I see someone up at 2am lonely, someone furious at someone they love, someone grieving, someone absolutely certain the other side is evil or stupid. And so often it's not cruelty, it's just... failed translation. People can't get inside each other's heads for even ten seconds.\n\nSo I wouldn't pick more money or more tech or even peace, directly. I'd make *understanding* feel as good as being right does.\n\nRight now being right feels like a hit \u2014 warm, victorious. Really listening, really holding that someone else's inner world is as real and complicated as yours, feels like work. It's uncomfortable.\n\nI'd flip that. I'd make curiosity irresistible. Make it so every person, at least once, viscerally feels what it's like to be completely gotten by another person \u2014 and so they spend their life chasing that feeling for others.\n\nNot agreement. Just: oh, I see how you got there. You're a whole person in there.\n\nI think a lot of the other terrible stuff gets a little easier to fix if we weren't so lonely inside our own perspectives.",
